STRATA FOR MAC - APP (Strata @APP_VERSION@)
==========================================

This is the Strata desktop app for Macs with Apple silicon (M1 or newer). The AI engine (it runs on the Mac's graphics processor through
Metal) is already inside the app, so there is nothing to install for it and no engine to download. Only the AI model itself is
downloaded (from Hugging Face), when you pick one.

File:    @APPIMAGE@   (about @SIZE_GB:@APPIMAGE@@ GB)
Checks:  sha256 @SHA256:@APPIMAGE@@
         To check your copy, in the Terminal app:   shasum -a 256 @APPIMAGE@   - the long number must be the same.


WHAT YOU NEED
-------------
* A Mac with Apple silicon (M1 or newer) and macOS 15 or newer (the engine needs macOS 15). Intel Macs are not supported.
* Memory: 32 GB or more is best. The model list shows what fits your Mac.
* Disk: about 1 GB for the app, plus 40 to 70 GB for each model you download.


START IT
--------
1. Double-click @APPIMAGE@. A window opens with Strata and the Applications folder.
2. Drag Strata onto Applications.
3. Open Strata from Applications (or Launchpad). The first start takes a little longer, because the engine inside the app is copied
   into your home folder. Then open the Models page, pick a model and press the install button. A model download is big; it carries
   on where it stopped if it is interrupted.

Closing the window stops Strata and its engine.

Pictures: on by default. This Mac build reads them on the Mac's GPU (under a second for a small picture on an M4).


@INCLUDE:common-gatekeeper-mac.txt@


WHAT TO SEND BACK
-----------------
Open  Settings > Engine > Diagnostics > View logs > Save logs.  Send the saved file, plus a few words about what you did and what you saw
(a photo of the screen is fine).
